# Character count

Show a remaining count only when a real limit applies to an answer.

These are civica.uk reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it for a bounded dashboard note or message field whose receiving system has a documented limit. Include that limit before the field, not just in a changing counter.

## When not to use it

Do not invent limits to make cards fit. Increase an unnecessary storage restriction instead of asking people to shorten useful instructions. Do not prevent pasting a complete answer.

## Home Assistant adaptation

The example uses the GOV.UK character-count enhancement. It allows editing beyond the limit and provides feedback; submission validation still belongs to the component that stores the note. A household note is not a monitored message to a support team. State its audience and purpose.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Keep the visible counter below the textarea. Associate hints and count with the field, retain the static maximum when JavaScript is unavailable, and avoid announcing every keystroke. The enhanced component schedules screen-reader updates.

